+// Story 043, tasks 3.1 and 6.3 — the launch decision, its refusals, drift, and the forwarded
+// memory port (R1.1, R1.3, R1.4, R1.5, R1.6, R1.7, R1.8, R1.9, R1.10, R1.11, R1.12, R3.8, R5.4,
+// R7.1, R7.2, R7.3; Q4). Wired in the crate root `src/agent_sandbox.rs` as
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     mod launch_tests;
+//
+// Validation filters: `launch` (3.1, every test path is `launch_tests::…`) and `launch_memory`
+// (6.3, the `launch_memory_*` tests).
+//
+// Contract (design.md §agent_sandbox::launch). Assumed signatures — adjust the `use`/call only:
+//   - `crate::launch::decide(agent_id: AgentId, project: &Entity<Project>, cmd: AgentServerCommand,
+//      cx: &mut AsyncApp) -> LaunchDecision` (async)
+//   - `LaunchDecision::{Jailed(LaunchRecord, AgentServerCommand), Unchanged(LaunchRecord), Refused(LaunchError)}`
+//   - `LaunchRecord { agent_id, project_root, reason: Reason, ai_jail_version: Option<Version>,
+//      rw_maps: Vec<PathBuf>, allow_hosts: Vec<String>, forward_ports: Vec<u16>, settings_fingerprint }`
+//   - `Reason::{On, Off, OwnCommand, Remote}`; `LaunchError: Display`
+//   - `crate::launch::drifted(&LaunchRecord, &AgentSandboxSettings) -> bool`
+//
+// The project is on the real filesystem (RealFs) because the fake `ai-jail` must run as a real
+// process and `.zed` creation must be observable on disk.
+//
+// Hostile halves first:
+//   - own command, wrongly COLLAPSE: `/opt/x/ai-jailer` and `/opt/x/ai-jail-wrapper` are NOT
+//     ai-jail and are wrapped; wrongly SPLIT: `ai-jail` under any directory is own-command, even
+//     with the sandbox off and with no managed ai-jail installed.
+//   - refusals, wrongly START: every refusal path (missing binary, unreadable version, missing
+//     Claude dir, invalid map, invalid host, unparsable memory endpoint) ends in `Refused` whose
+//     text ends with "The agent was not started without the sandbox." and names the cause.
+//   - dedup, wrongly SPLIT: the same folder spelled through a symlink, with a trailing slash, or
+//     equal to the Claude config dir appears once as `--rw-map`.
+//   - drift, wrongly COLLAPSE: another project's change is not drift for this one; wrongly
+//     SPLIT: reverting the change clears the drift.
+//   - memory port, wrongly FORWARD: a non-loopback endpoint, or one whose host merely starts with
+//     `127.0.0.1`/`localhost`, adds no `--forward-port`; memory off adds none.
+
+use std::os::unix::fs::{PermissionsExt as _, symlink};
+use std::path::{Path, PathBuf};
+
+use collections::HashMap;
+use fs::RealFs;
+use gpui::{AppContext as _, Entity, TestAppContext, UpdateGlobal as _};
+use project::Project;
+use project::agent_registry_store::ZEO_PLUS_AGENT_ID;
+use project::agent_server_store::{AgentId, AgentServerCommand};
+use serde_json::{Value, json};
+use settings::{Settings as _, SettingsStore};
+
+use crate::AgentSandboxSettings;
+use crate::launch::{LaunchDecision, LaunchRecord, Reason, decide, drifted};
+
