+// Story 043, task 6.2 — the ai-memory MCP client, its response parsers against the fixtures
+// captured on 2026-10-10, errors, auth and logs (R6.1, R6.5, R6.6, R6.8, R6.9, R7.1, R7.3, R9.3,
+// R9.4; Q4, Q13, Q14). Wired in the crate root `src/agent_sandbox.rs` as
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     mod memory_tests;
+//
+// Validation filter: `memory` (every test path is `memory_tests::…`).
+//
+// The fake ai-memory is an MCP streamable-HTTP server built on `http_client::FakeHttpClient`
+// (the same seam context_server's own HttpTransport tests use), so the real `ContextServer::http`
+// transport, headers and JSON-RPC framing are exercised.
+//
+// Contract (design.md §agent_sandbox::memory, §Data Models). Assumed signatures — adjust the
+// `use`/constructor only:
+//   - `crate::memory::MemoryClient::new(endpoint: Url, auth_token: Option<String>,
+//      http_client: Arc<dyn HttpClient>, cx: &AsyncApp) -> anyhow::Result<MemoryClient>`
+//     (production passes `std::env::var("AI_MEMORY_AUTH_TOKEN").ok()`)
+//   - `status(&self, &MemoryScope) -> Result<MemoryStatus, MemoryError>`,
+//     `recent(&self, &MemoryScope, limit: usize) -> Result<Vec<RecentPage>, MemoryError>`,
+//     `delete(&self, &MemoryScope, path: &str) -> Result<(), MemoryError>` (all async)
+//   - `MemoryStatus { server_version: String, endpoint, scope: MemoryScope, pages: u64, sessions: u64 }`
+//     — `pages` is `counts.pages_latest` (the live pages; `pages_all` counts every version)
+//   - `RecentPage { path: String, title: String, .. }`
+//   - `MemoryError::{Unreachable { endpoint }, Timeout, UnknownProject { scope }, Server(String), Malformed}`
+//     with the R6.6/R6.8 texts as `Display`
+//   - `crate::memory::forward_port(&Url) -> Option<u16>`
+//
+// Hostile halves first:
+//   - unknown project, wrongly COLLAPSE: the server's *workspace* not-found error (the scope
+//     naming gotcha) is a server error with its text, not "No memory recorded …".
+//   - timeout, both sides: no answer within 5 s is `Timeout`; an answer at 4 s is a result.
+//   - malformed, wrongly PANIC/ACCEPT: non-JSON text, a missing field, empty content.
+//   - loopback, wrongly FORWARD: `127.0.0.1.example.com`, `localhost.example.com`, a LAN IP
+//     (only `127.0.0.1`, `::1` and `localhost` are loopback here); wrongly REFUSE: `[::1]`,
+//     `localhost`, and an endpoint with no explicit port (its scheme default).
+//   - token, wrongly LEAK: the bearer token is on every request and in no log line; no page
+//     snippet is logged.
