+// Story 043, tasks 4.1 and 8.1 — the thread's jail icon (R1.7, R1.8, R5.1–R5.7) and the palette
+// actions (R8.1–R8.4). Wired in the crate root `src/agent_ui.rs` as
+//
+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     mod agent_jail_status_tests;
+//
+// Test paths are `agent_jail_status_tests::icon::…` and
+// `agent_jail_status_tests::agent_sandbox_actions::…`, so the Validation filters
+// `agent_jail_status` (4.1) and `agent_sandbox_actions` (8.1) select them.
+//
+// Contract (design.md §Toolbar icon, §Palette actions, §launch). Assumed signatures — adjust the
+// `use`/call only:
+//   - `agent_sandbox::launch::{LaunchRecord, LaunchRegistry, Reason}`; `LaunchRegistry::register(record, cx)`
+//   - `ThreadView::render_agent_jail_status(&mut self, cx) -> Option<AnyElement>`
+//   - the icon's presentation is computed by a pure seam the render calls:
+//     `crate::agent_jail_status::jail_status_summary(record: &LaunchRecord, drifted: bool)
+//      -> JailStatusSummary { icon: IconName, color: Color, lines: Vec<SharedString> }`
+//     (the tooltip shows `lines`; the IconButton uses `icon`/`color`). GPUI exposes no text query
+//     on a rendered tooltip, so this seam is where R5.2–R5.6 are asserted; the rendered panel is
+//     asserted through `IconButton`'s automatic `ICON-<name>` debug selector.
+//   - `zed_actions::AGENT_JAIL_SETTINGS_PATH == "agent_sandbox"`
+//   - `agent_sandbox::{Toggle}` / `agent_memory::{Status, OpenProjectMemory}` action types, at
+//     `crate::agent_sandbox_actions::{Toggle, Status, OpenProjectMemory}` or wherever declared.
+//
+// Hostile halves first:
+//   - icon key, wrongly COLLAPSE: a record for `/w/app2` draws nothing on a thread of `/w/app`;
+//     no record (agent still loading) draws nothing.
+//   - state, wrongly CLOSED: Off and Remote draw the open lock; wrongly OPEN: OwnCommand draws
+//     the closed lock; outdated draws the warning colour, never the default.
+//   - native thread, wrongly DOUBLE: a native thread never gets the jail icon.
+//   - toggle, wrongly SILENT-OFF: the palette's off path asks the same confirmation and Cancel
+//     writes nothing; wrongly ACT: with no local project nothing changes.
