+//     #[cfg(test)]
+//     #[path = "agent_jail_page_tests.rs"]
+//     mod agent_jail_page_tests;
+//
+// Test paths are `…::agent_jail_page_tests::page::…` and `…::agent_jail_page_tests::agent_memory_section::…`,
+// so the Validation filters `agent_jail_page` (5.2) and `agent_memory_section` (7.1) select them.
+//
+// Contract (design.md §Settings sub-page, §agent_sandbox::memory). The registration is asserted
+// on the real `page_data::settings_data`. GPUI offers no text query on rendered elements, so the
+// page's text-bearing decisions are asserted on the functions the render calls. Assumed seams —
+// adjust the `use`/call only, keep the assertions:
+//   - `super::banner_text(installed: Option<&semver::Version>) -> Option<String>` — `None` means
+//     ai-jail was not found (R3.6), an outdated version gives the R3.5 warning, a safe one none.
+//   - `super::project_notice(root: Option<&Path>) -> Option<&'static str>` — R3.3.
+//   - `super::add_entry(kind: EntryKind, root: &Path, raw: &str, cx: &mut App) -> Task<Result<(), String>>`
+//     and `super::remove_entry(kind, root, raw, cx) -> Task<Result<(), String>>`, with
+//     `EntryKind::{RwMap, AllowHost}`: validate (task 2.1), write `projects[root]` through
+//     `update_settings_file`, or return the rule text and write nothing (R3.4, R4.4).
+//   - `super::AgentMemorySection` (an entity): `new(root: Option<PathBuf>, window, cx)` using the
+//     user `agent_memory` settings and `cx.http_client()`; `refresh(&mut self, cx)`;
+//     `forget(&mut self, path: &str, window, cx)`; read-outs `status_line() -> Option<String>`,
+//     `error_line() -> Option<String>`, `pages() -> &[RecentPage]`, `endpoint_note() -> Option<String>`.
+//
+// Hostile halves first:
+//   - entries, wrongly WRITE: a refused entry leaves the settings file byte-identical; wrongly
+//     ASK: adding and removing never prompt.
+//   - banner, wrongly SILENT: missing → install hint; outdated → both advisories; wrongly NOISY:
+//     a safe version (including 10.0.0) shows none.
+//   - memory, wrongly CALL: memory off makes zero requests; a cancelled Forget sends no delete;
+//     an error is never retried in the background.
+
